FILED + FIXED s532c (Opus agent, 2026-11-06), the board hunt of #4087 (Template-Toolkit proc.t).

    no strict 'refs';
    my $proxy = "Proxy::X";
    print defined(*{ $proxy . "::new" }) ? "def" : "undef", "\n";
    unless (defined(*{ $proxy . "::new" })) { *{ $proxy . "::new" } = sub { bless \my $t, $_[0] } }
    print ref(Proxy::X->new), "\n";

  perl 5.40.3: undef / Proxy::X.   PCL (ce665621): def, then dies "Can't locate object method "new" via package "Proxy::X"".

MECHANISM: the `defined` lowering had no arm for a `*` Cast, so `defined *{EXPR}` emitted `(p-defined (p-dynamic-typeglob EXPR))` -- and p-dynamic-typeglob MAKES the glob (and the package), so the answer was always 1.  perl's rv2gv under `defined` carries OPpDONT_INIT_GV: nothing is created and the answer is whether the GV exists.  Template::Plugin::Procedural::load installs its proxy's AUTOLOAD and `new` only `unless defined *{"${proxy}::..."}`, so every procedural plugin (TT t/lib ProcFoo / ProcBar) died at `USE`.

FIX (s532c): `Pl/ExprToCL.pm`'s `defined` arm lowers a `*` Cast operand (`_cast_operand_id`, the `&`-Cast shape test generalised) to `(p-glob-defined EXPR)`; `cl/pcl-runtime.lisp` `p-glob-defined` answers true for a glob value / glob ref / handle, the forced-main names (`*p-forced-main-names*`, now shared with %p-select-glob-name), and a NAME whose package's stash holds the entry by p-stash's own per-symbol rule (`%p-stash-has-entry-p`: a sub with a body, a variable / filehandle %p-stash-variable-name names).  Creates nothing.  Guard `Pl/t/glob-defined-01.t` row 1 (17 spellings vs perl; FAILS on ce665621).
RESIDUE (not chased): a glob perl creates by a mere compile-time MENTION (`zz() if 0;` makes *zz) or by a forward declaration `sub f;` -- p-stash's view does not list a declaration-only stub, so `defined *{"f"}` answers false where perl says true.

